---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/winback';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/winback');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/winback');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When is a customer lapsed?",
    "answer": "When the buying cycle and available order history justify that conclusion. Use category and seasonal context rather than a universal day count."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is winback the same as re-engagement?",
    "answer": "No. Winback concerns repeat purchase; re-engagement concerns continued interest in messages. A person can be commercially lapsed and still want the newsletter."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should a purchase stop winback?",
    "answer": "Recheck the new order and stop acquisition messages it makes irrelevant. Include relevant sales channels so offline purchases do not create false lapse."
  },
  {
    "question": "How often can the same buyer re-enter?",
    "answer": "Set an explicit cycle and re-entry policy. Do not restart indefinitely from an unchanged old lapse condition."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24"><div class="container">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Winback</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email tools for winback campaigns</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Winback addresses a previous buyer whose next purchase may be overdue. That differs from newsletter re-engagement and from replenishment of a known consumable. Establish why another purchase is plausible before scheduling a reminder.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary mt-9" href="/apps">Compare the tool catalog</a>
  </div></section>
  <article class="container pb-16 space-y-12">
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Define lapse from the buying cycle</h2>
      <p>Review repeat purchase intervals by product and customer type, accounting for seasonality and recent cohorts that have not had time to return. Durable goods and annual gifts do not share the same lapse clock as consumables. A missing order in one integration can also create a false lapse.</p>
      <p>Klaviyo documents an order-triggered winback flow with a delay and a filter checking for no new order since entering. Use that as a mechanism to evaluate, not evidence for one universal delay. Reconcile other sales channels that matter to your business before telling a customer they have been away.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Distinguish purchase lapse from lost interest</h2>
      <p>A buyer who reads a newsletter or updates a preference may want a relevant release rather than a generic return coupon. A customer without reliable engagement signals needs a separate deliverability and permission decision. Do not treat a tracked open as proof of intent or absence of opens as proof of indifference.</p>
      <p>For a proposed luggage campaign, a previous suitcase buyer may need a compatible accessory or repair resource, not another suitcase. If there is no credible next purchase, leave them in a suitable content program or pause promotions. Do not manufacture urgency by claiming their relationship is expiring.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Reset after the relevant state changes</h2>
      <p>Check for a new order before each acquisition message. Resolve overlaps with replenishment, an active subscription, a pending replacement or an unresolved service problem. A skipped subscription shipment is not equivalent to cancellation; use the subscription authority for that distinction.</p>
      <p>Record the completed lapse cycle and a deliberate re-entry policy. A flow that finishes without a purchase should not restart merely because the customer still matches the same old condition. A new relevant event or a defined review point can justify another decision without endless repeating offers.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose a reason to return before an incentive</h2>
      <p>Offer a real change: a compatible addition, a useful new collection or an invitation that matches the previous relationship. Treat former VIPs with accurate recognition, while respecting current benefit terms. Prior use of a code alone does not prove a person would never buy at full price.</p>
      <p>If testing an incentive, keep eligibility, code restrictions and contribution costs explicit. Compare it with relevant content or no additional winback where feasible. Stop or revise a path if complaints or fulfilment problems appear; a larger attributed revenue number cannot settle that decision alone.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Evaluate resets and incremental value</h2>
      <p>Ask Klaviyo, Sequenzy, Drip, Omnisend or your existing platform to demonstrate the lapse definition using your order channels and exclusions. Compare the ability to explain a skipped message and prevent accidental re-entry, rather than selecting a winner from an assumed predictive score.</p>
      <p>A proposed exercise places an order during a delay, adds an offline purchase and completes a cycle without ordering. Verify resets and re-entry decisions. Measure eligible-customer repeat purchase over the same observation window for treatment and comparison groups; report incentive costs and complaints. These are suggested checks, not observed merchant outcomes.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Reference and related workflows</h2>
      <p>Product reference: <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002775192">Klaviyo winback flow setup</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed exercises above are editorial guidance.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">replenishment</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/vip-segments">vip segments</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Winback FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
